        /// <summary>
        /// Adds raw PLY data directly to the Work Order&#39;s Display List and Process Step List. Accepts projection data in raw coordinates (same as Work Order PLY files). When projecting, Iris will sweep from the first point to the last (if you want a closed polygon, repeat the first coordinate as the last)  See \&quot;Ad-Hoc Projection Entities\&quot; in the Integrators Guide for why/when you&#39;d want to use this vs. &#x60;/ProjectEntities&#x60;  Any projections added here (with a name provided) show in the Iris Process Step List (if Iris is open), are visualized in the 3D/CAD view and are automatically projected by the appropriate lasers.  Projections added via API show as dark green in the 3D/CAD view, and the selection  highlight in the Process Step List is dark green as well (steps that existed in the Work Order when opened are highlighted in light green).    Steps added via &#x60;/AddProjectPolygon&#x60; immediately replace any contents of the Work Order&#39;s Display List. Note that if you do not provide a Name, the new step is NOT added to the Work Order&#39;s Process Step List.  Selection of steps in the Work Order&#39;s Process Step List is unaffected by this method; Next/Previous commands will still be operating on whichever steps were previously selected (in an open Iris Client, or using &#x60;/SetCurrentSelectionSteps&#x60;.)    * **Name** - If provided, is the ply name as shown in Iris&#39; Process Step List; does not have to be unique; methods that require named process steps (like &#x60;/RemoveProjectPolygons&#x60; and &#x60;/RemoveEntities&#x60;) may not behave as expected if the specified process step exists more than once; in most cases, the first occurrence of that step name will be addressed only. Where duplicate step or layer names are expected, &#x60;EntityUniqueID&#x60; specific endpoints (e.g. &#x60;/RemoveEntitiesWithID&#x60;, &#x60;/RemoveProjectPolygonsWithId&#x60;) can be used, after retrieving step and layer &#x60;EntityUniqueID&#x60; values using &#x60;/GetCurrentProjectionEntities&#x60; or &#x60;/GetWorkOrderEntityAccessInfo&#x60;.  * **ID** - Corresponds to EntityUniqueID; the identifier that uniquely identifies steps - MUST be unique in the Work Order. If not provided, is created and assigned automatically. This is the parameter used by &#x60;/RemoveProjectPolygonsWithId&#x60;.  * **Units** - Units the projection points in &#39;NormalPointsData&#39; are specified in; does not have to match that of the open Work Order, Iris will convert; see \&quot;Units\&quot; in Integrators Guide  * **Type** - use \&quot;Polygon\&quot;; other values are unsupported at this time.  * **NormalPointsData** - string containing raw projection coordinates (.ply file format), one line per projection point with 2,3 or 6 values space separated: 2 values &#x3D; 2D point (z&#x3D;0)  3 values &#x3D; 3D point (x,y,z); 6 values &#x3D; 3D point (x,y,z) with normal vector (a,b,c - do not have to be normalized)    &lt;example&gt;               0.684006 9.976661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               1.242432 9.976661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               1.242432 6.380219 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               3.505415 6.380219 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               3.505415 9.976661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               4.387138 9.976661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               4.387138 8.162716 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               6.938428 8.162716 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               6.938428 11.082913 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               5.713986 11.082913 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               5.713986 11.582541 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               7.913908 11.582541 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               7.913908 15.575661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               3.505415 15.575661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               3.505415 13.949827 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               0.684006 13.949827 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               0.684006 9.976661 0.100000 0.000000 0.000000 1               &lt;/example&gt;    **Note** - step and layer \&quot;uniqueness\&quot; and the behaviour of this method depends on BOTH the step/layer NAME (argument &#x60;Name&#x60;) and its unique Identifier EntityUniqueId (argument &#x60;Id&#x60;).   If you specify:   EXISTING/NO Name + EXISTING Id - this is IGNORED; to \&quot;switch\&quot; to an existing step with either Name or Id, use &#x60;/AddEntity&#x60;.  EXISTING Name + NEW Id - creates new (duplicate) step named Name; discards the provided Id and auto-generates new one  EXISTING Name + NO Id - creates new (duplicate) step named Name; auto-generates the Id  NEW Name + EXISTING Id - creates new (new) step named Name; IGNORES the provided Id and auto-generates new one  NEW Name + NEW Id - creates new (new) step named Name; IGNORES the provided Id and auto-generates new one  NEW Name + NO Id - creates a new step named Name, auto-generates Id  See \&quot;Process Step Uniqueness\&quot; in the Integrator&#39;s Guide for more details. Also note that any Id (EntityUniqueId) automatically generated will be decreasing integrators (-1, -2, -3)...
        /// </summary>
        /// <exception cref="VisionAndProjectionService.Swagger.Client.ApiException">Thrown when fails to make API call</exception>
        /// <param name="projectPolygon"></param>
        /// <returns>ResultDtoString</returns>
        public ResultDtoString CoreLaserServiceAddProjectPolygon (ProjectPolygonDto projectPolygon)
        {
             ApiResponse<ResultDtoString> localVarResponse = CoreLaserServiceAddProjectPolygonWithHttpInfo(projectPolygon);
             return localVarResponse.Data;
        }

