n in the collection that can be toggled off and on with the Options &amp;gt; Crosshairs feature.     **TextBlock** - Projected Text - both the text to display itself, and 3 points to define the origin, orientation, and projection plane of the Projected Text chevron (the angle icon used to locate and toggle Projected Text. The 3 coordinates of the chevron, in order, are bottom-left, vertex, and upper-left. The plane defined by the coordinates of the text chevron becomes the projection plane for the text. The size of the chevron is used for text size. Only a subset of ASCII characters are supported by the Projected Text laser font: &#x60;a-z A-Z 0-9 \\_ . , ? \\! ; : \\- \\+ \\* / \\\\ \\| \\( \\) { } [ ] \\# @ \\~ &#x60;. For more information on defining projected text see \&quot;Iris Authoring\&quot; in the Operator Guide.    **ActionType** - (optional) the step actions to be tracked for these entities. This section can be removed for &#39;ProjectOnly&#39; operations, or use &#39;Polygon&#39;.  Legal actions are from the supported ply actions in the Iris Authoring Guide.    **AdditionalProperties** - (optional) a dictionary capable of holding any properties that don&#39;t fit into a set category.   For example, the duration of a countdown timer.   This section can be removed for &#39;ProjectOnly&#39; operations    * **Operation** - Typically use &#39;ProjectSkipInspectingCurrent&#39; for updating the projection.  Other options are &#39;UpdateDisplayOnly&#39; for client UI updates, &#39;ProjectAfterInspectingCurrent&#39; for updating multiple services when adding a camera action, &#39;ProjectOnly&#39; for projector projection update only (currently only pick n project is using this flag), and &#39;ProjectAfterLoggingInfo&#39;.    * **ActionOverrideInfo** - (optional) the user override information for failed inspection actions.  This section can be removed for &#39;ProjectOnly&#39; operations.    * **ActionTrackInfo** - (optional) the display step actions to be tracked before project the new entities.  This section can be removed for &#39;ProjectOnly&#39; operations.    * **EntityUniqueId** - the unique ID of the step; if creating a new ad hoc step this must be distinct from any ids already in use by the system; ids can be retrieved using &#x60;/GetCurrentProjectionEntities&#x60; or &#x60;/GetProjectionData&#x60; if needed.    * **EntityName** - the name of the step; if the step name specified is NOT unique, the first step that matches the name is used; must match the EntityUniqueId if modifying an existing step.  See \&quot;Ad-hoc Projections\&quot; in the Integrators Reference.    (1) *No changes to the Process Step List, projection (&#x60;.ply&#x60;) file made by this endpoint will be saved, even if the Work Order is saved in Iris Client.*
